\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids runs from 1951 to 2025, and July to August came in under 90% of normal in 33 of those 75 years. In 2025 that same pair fell to 42% of normal on the middle of the grids, and August to September was 56%. So far in 2026, January to February came in at 51% and March to April at 149%. Grid 25104 had its driest year in 1988 at 72% of normal.</p>"}
